WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.801
-Welcome, welcome, welcome, to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.000
You're here. You're watching at home.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.367
Thank you very much.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.267
[ Cheers and applause ] Very excited.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:10.100
Very exciting here in the building.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.868
The one and only Serena Williams is my guest tonight!

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.734
♪♪

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.167
All day, my staff was like,

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.033
"I can't believe the greatest of all time is here."

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.234
And I said, "Thanks, but tonight is about Serena."

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:26.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.367
Serena Williams and I have so much in common.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:31.634
She wrote a children's book. I wrote a children's book.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:35.634
She's a sports legend, role model, and a fashion icon.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:39.100
I wrote a children's book. You know.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.467
Last month, Serena announced

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:43.300
that she's evolving away from tennis.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.934
But if we're lucky, she'll pull a Tom Brady

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.400
and evolve right back in three weeks.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.367
What do you say, huh? Can we get her to do it?

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.267
Have her announce on the show tonight.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.400
Let's get to some news.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.868
Well, people are talking about this.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.801
On Sunday, former president Trump was spotted in DC,

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.934
but nobody knew why he was there.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.634
And then yesterday, he was seen at his Virginia golf course

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.467
with a big group of people, but they weren't playing golf.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.934
[ Audience oohs ] They were just touring

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.434
around the course talking.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:14.200
Here's a photo. Yeah.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.667
Looks like backstage at a fashion show for Marshall's.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.868
Look at that.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.501
Very diverse group.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.200
They had polo shirts of every color.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.534
They really -- Trump was like,

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.934
"So, I think I buried the documents somewhere around here.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:30.667
So start -- start diggin', boys!"

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.000
Yeah, Trump was smart.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.067
He was like, "How about nine of us meet on the green

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.701
with no clubs so it doesn't look suspicious?"

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.501
Speaking of the former president,

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.934
I read that the National Archives still doesn't know

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.267
whether they have all of the presidential records

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.734
that Trump took from the White House.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.801
Amazing. Somehow my library knows

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:49.601
I've had a copy of "Goodnight Moon" for 40 years,

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.300
but we still can't track down these documents.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.400
Where are these documents?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.467
How did they even find my address?

00:01:56.467 --> 00:02:00.300
[ Applause ]

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.534
Well, some news from the UK.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.901
King Charles is still adjusting to his new role.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.701
And yesterday, we showed a clip of him

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:09.334
getting angry over some extra pens on his desk.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.400
In case you missed it, here's the clip.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.734
Look at this. Yeah.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.000
Ehh!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.133
Ehh!

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:25.968
He was not happy.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.801
Let's check in to see if things have gotten better for him.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:30.767
By the way, this is real. This is a clip from today.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:08.033
[ Applause ]

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.000
If this were baseball, Prince William would already

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.167
be warming up in the bullpen. You know what I'm talking about?

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.534
He's like, "Alright."

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.701
Everyone was quickly like, "It's okay, Your Majesty.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.267
Pens are hard."

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.000
Writing the wrong date, pens leaking on him.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.200
Honestly, royalty has never been more relatable.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.667
Hey, get this.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.968
I saw that due to Russia's invasion of Ukraine,

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:30.834
Vladimir Putin will not be invited to the Queen's funeral.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.234
Apparently, Putin is okay with it.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:33.734
He was afraid he was going to sit next

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.467
to that raging lunatic, King Charles.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.901
[as Putin] "He doesn't like pens.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.267
Keep the pens away from him."

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.033
But Putin said he'll still be there in spirit...

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.634
and in a tiny recording device in the bouquet.

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:49.100
Switching gears, Apple just released a new software update

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.634
that lets you edit and unsend messages.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.434
Yeah, and this is nice -- after your third time

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:55.601
editing a message, you get a notification that says,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.367
"You're drunk. Go to bed."

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.667
Some more business news.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.734
Peloton's been having a tough year,

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.200
and they just announced that their co-founders

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.200
are leaving the company.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.534
It was time for a change.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.767
Peloton's been stationary for too long.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:13.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.267
♪♪

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.167
I love ya.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.868
The Peloton co-founders would have left sooner,

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.968
but they couldn't unclip their shoes.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.434
"Gosh. Why am I..."

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:31.901
Of course, since it's Peloton,

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.200
they're not getting rid of their founders.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.801
They're just gonna push them to the corner of the room

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.601
and use them as a coat rack. Hey, did you guys see this?

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:40.834
A Starbucks canned beverage has been recalled in seven states

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.901
because they could contain metal fragments.

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:47.434
Or as Starbucks put it, "Now introducing tetanus spice!"

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:48.901
On the plus side,

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:51.968
the jagged metal pieces really do wake you up.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.267
Well, this is going viral.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.634
A Ryanair passenger tweeted at the airline

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.634
complaining that she paid for a window seat

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:58.834
and didn't get one.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:00.801
And here's the photo that she tweeted.

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.567
Alright.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:03.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.467
And here's Ryanair's response. This is real.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.901
[ Laughter ] "You want a window?

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:14.501
You want to talk -- You wanna play window game?

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:15.868
You wanna play window?"

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:18.334
[ Applause ]

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.734
Meanwhile, if you ask for a window seat on Spirit Airlines,

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.467
they give you a drill and some Saran wrap.

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:24.734
They go, "Oh, just go for it."

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:27.834
Hey, I heard about a woman who was fined $1,000

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.434
for trying to smuggle 50 wheels of cheese

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:34.901
across the border into the US.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:38.067
Oh, this joke is gonna get me thrown out of the building.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.067
Are you ready? -Yeah.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:43.033
-50 wheels of cheese. They fined her.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:45.667
Okay. Drum roll, I guess.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.567
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:49.634
They gave her a $1,000 fine and said,

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.300
"Never fondue it again."

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.501
That's it. That's all. We got it.

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:54.634
-Get out! Get outta here!

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.868 --> 00:06:01.667
♪♪

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:04.801
[British accent] These pens! Ah! These bloody things!

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:08.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.334
Guys, finally it is Tuesday. It's time for "WeTweet."

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:11.567
Here we go.

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:14.601
-♪ WeTweet ♪

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:17.734
♪ WeTweet ♪

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.133
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:22.868
This is where we, as a group,

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:25.400
decide something that we should post on Twitter.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.801
I'm going to show you five different tweets,

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:27.667
and we're all going to vote on

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.234
whether you like each one or not.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:31.534
You all have your voting clickers at your seats.

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:33.767
You can all vote -- Yeah.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.167
That's probably yours, yeah.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.601
[ Laughter ] You can vote for all of them.

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:38.834
You can vote for none of them.

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:40.334
Whatever you want. I just want you to have fun.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.634
We're going to see the results live.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:42.767
Tariq, Roots?

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:43.901
Tariq, you have your clicker?

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:45.501
-Yeah, I'm done already, thanks.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:46.667
-No, no, we didn't even start --

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.300
We didn't even start the game yet.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.634
-Wait, what? -We didn't start the game yet.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.100
Don't vote on Tariq's -- -Can you unvote?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.200
-No, you can't unvote either, no.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.634
Whatever tweet gets the most likes,

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:58.534
we will tweet it out live on the show on a commercial break

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:00.801
so you can all like it and "wetweet" it.

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:03.300
[ Audience ahs ] Yeah, it's a shared experience.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.634
You guys ready for this?

00:07:04.634 --> 00:07:05.701
[ Cheers ]

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.200
Our first tweet is...

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:16.667
-I didn't like that one. -You didn't like it?

00:07:16.667 --> 00:07:20.467
-Nope. -I think it's alright.

00:07:20.467 --> 00:07:22.167
I mean, I kind of get it. -I dig it.

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:24.567
-You dig it?

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:25.667
Alright. The votes are in.

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:28.133
Let's see the results here.

00:07:28.133 --> 00:07:31.200
Ooh. Wow. [ Sad tuba ]

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.467
Very honest audience.

00:07:32.467 --> 00:07:34.267
They did not enjoy that one.

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:35.734
[ Laughter ] They did not like that one.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:37.367
It's okay. We have a couple more.

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:38.467
Here we go.

00:07:38.467 --> 00:07:39.968
-We're warming up. -Yeah, we're warming up.

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:45.767
This next one is...

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:48.000
-Thinker.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.834
-I can tell by people's eyes that they're saying, "No."

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:54.000
[ Laughter ] They're masked.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.367
And they're just looking at me like --

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:58.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:00.167
I can tell they pressed no.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.400
I'm going to say this one is --

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.200
What was the last one, how many no's?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.200
76 likes?

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.934
So I'm going to say this one is probably

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:11.100
in the 150 range of "no."

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.834
[ Laughter ] -Ah.

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:15.701
-This might be one of the worst ones ever.

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:16.901
Let's see the results.

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:20.000
[ Sad tuba ] Yeah. Very close. I felt it.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.400
I knew it. I could tell.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.400
They looked at me like, "No, Jimmy, not going to do it.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.501
I'm going to let you drown a little bit, then I'll save you."

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:27.467
I go, "Alright, teach me a lesson."

00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:28.767
How about this next one here?

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:40.033
-Yes, you do. You know you do.

00:08:40.033 --> 00:08:43.968
-I do, but is that more fact than it is funny?

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:45.300
-It's a fun fact.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.000
-I always start at chapter four.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.367
-What? -I don't want to hear

00:08:49.367 --> 00:08:52.334
about their childhood, and when they discovered music.

00:08:52.334 --> 00:08:53.767
-I don't want to hear about that either.

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:55.367
"My mom was born --" I go, "Hey, if I want to read

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.234
about your mom, I would get her biography."

00:08:57.234 --> 00:08:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.534 --> 00:09:01.033
I think we're riding this train together.

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:03.601
And I think that we're 50/50 on this.

00:09:03.601 --> 00:09:06.567
I think we're split down the middle, if I'm being nice.

00:09:06.567 --> 00:09:09.601
Let's see the results.

00:09:09.601 --> 00:09:11.000
What?

00:09:12.234 --> 00:09:14.667
I feel like I don't know you anymore.

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:16.434
What happened to us?

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:17.968
We had something.

00:09:17.968 --> 00:09:19.567
-Wait, you didn't want them to like that?

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.167
-No, I like that they liked it.

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.601
I just didn't expect them to like it.

00:09:22.601 --> 00:09:24.601
I liked it.

00:09:24.601 --> 00:09:26.267
I mean, we both did the same thing.

00:09:26.267 --> 00:09:29.701
I just thought the numbers would be more even.

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:31.167
This one's pretty good.

00:09:33.067 --> 00:09:35.067
What do you think about this one before I say it?

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:39.133
-Hated it. [ Laughter ]

00:09:39.133 --> 00:09:40.167
-Next up...

00:09:45.901 --> 00:09:48.000
-I always say that. -Oh.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.300
Why not, man?

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:51.100
I don't know if I'm happy, but just do it,

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.601
and you probably end up happy.

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:55.100
I think this one's up there. -This is the winner.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.167
-The winner? The last one was pretty good too.

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:58.434
I think this one is going to be the winner.

00:09:58.434 --> 00:10:00.834
Let's see the results on this one right here.

00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:05.467
Oh, yeah! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:05.467 --> 00:10:09.868
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah. That's a good one.

00:10:09.868 --> 00:10:11.200
But this last one is pretty good, too.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.400
But that one's going to be the winner, I think.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.634
But this last one's good. Check this one out.

00:10:18.234 --> 00:10:21.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.267 --> 00:10:24.100
I mean, it kind of just goes in the floor.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.467
The floor eats it.

00:10:25.467 --> 00:10:27.801
-You find it months later. -You find it years later.

00:10:27.801 --> 00:10:29.033
Dried.

00:10:29.033 --> 00:10:31.701
"Honey, did you drop this bead?" -Right.

00:10:31.701 --> 00:10:33.934
-Yeah, I liked that one but I don't know if it's gonna be --

00:10:33.934 --> 00:10:35.734
What was the last record?

00:10:35.734 --> 00:10:36.934
-184. -184.

00:10:36.934 --> 00:10:38.734
It's got to beat 184. It's gotta be a good one.

00:10:38.734 --> 00:10:39.934
I don't know if it's going to happen.

00:10:39.934 --> 00:10:42.534
Let's see the results.

00:10:42.534 --> 00:10:44.400
No. It did not win!

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.000
[ Dinging ] It was high, but did not win.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.434
The winner was tweet number four.

00:10:48.434 --> 00:10:50.801
[ Dinging ]

00:10:50.801 --> 00:10:53.734
You should still clap your hands just in case.

00:10:53.734 --> 00:10:55.901
I will post this during the commercial break.

00:10:55.901 --> 00:10:57.200
If you see it on your feed,

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.934
give it a like, give it a wetweet.

00:10:58.934 --> 00:11:00.634
Why not? Enjoy.

